infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Coordinating a saga: choreography vs orchestration
  desc Choreography fits short 2-3 step flows; orchestration wins when the flow is long, branchy, or needs visibility
  compares
    - label Choreography
      children
        - label No central coordinator
          desc Each service reacts to an event and emits the next
        - label Zero new components, zero shared state
          desc Nothing extra to build or run
        - label Best for short 2-3 step flows
          desc Simple while the chain stays tiny
        - label The flow lives nowhere in code
          desc Reconstruct it from five services' handlers
        - label Debug across five event logs
          desc It rots as the flow grows
    - label Orchestration
      children
        - label Central orchestrator owns the flow
          desc One component sends explicit commands
        - label Another component to build and run
          desc The price of centralization
        - label Best when long, branchy, or visible
          desc Worth it for flows you debug at 3am
        - label The whole flow in one place
          desc Explicit, observable, testable, restartable
        - label Saga state in a queryable table
          desc Answer "where is this saga right now?"
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
